course: dictionary
lesson: 6770
title: Opponent: the other side
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An opponent is the person or team you play, compete or fight against. It can also mean someone who disagrees with an idea or plan and argues against it. «Ben shook hands with his opponent before the match.» Shaking hands shows that a game is a contest, not a fight.
explain: Context helps you work out which meaning fits. «Computer players in games are AI opponents» tells you an opponent can be a computer. «Opponents of the new law» tells you an opponent can be a person who argues against something, not only someone you play against.
explain: Good sportsmanship means treating your opponent fairly and with respect, even when you want to win. Respecting an opponent does not mean agreeing with them. You can respect someone and still disagree.
explain: Steel-manning is a good example. Before you reply to an opponent, you state their view in its strongest form. A straw man does the opposite: it is a weak, silly copy of what they said, which is easy to knock down.
fact: An opponent is a person or team you play, compete or fight against.
fact: An opponent can also be a person who disagrees with an idea or plan and argues against it.
fact: «Your opponent's move» means the move made by the person you are playing against in a board game such as chess.
fact: A «straw man» is a scarecrow version of what your opponent said: a silly copy that is easy to knock down.
fact: «Steel-manning» means stating the other side's view in its strongest form, which is fair to your opponent.
exercise: «Shake hands with your opponent before the game.» What is an opponent? | A player who never plays a match | *A person or team you play or compete against | A coach who picks the team | A referee who blows the whistle
exercise: «Computer players in games are AI opponents.» What does this tell you about opponents? | *An opponent can be a computer | An opponent is always a close friend | An opponent must always be a child | Opponents only exist in football
exercise: A councillor says, «I will answer the opponents of the new park.» Who are the opponents here? | People who sell ice cream in the park | *People who argue against the plan | People who play football in the park | People who build the park
test: In chess, «your opponent's move» means | A move the referee makes | The move you make yourself | A move that is always a mistake | *The move made by the person you are playing against
test: Which is the best way to treat an opponent in sport? | Tell them they cheated before the game starts | Be unkind and rude when you are losing | Ignore them completely, as if they are not there | *Shake hands and show good sportsmanship
exam: A straw man is best described as | A fair copy of your opponent's exact words | A kind of sports ball | A strong argument that is very hard to beat | *A scarecrow version of what your opponent said, easy to knock down
